Niagara adds explicit device placement and tensor-program execution to Caskade.

Caskade is by Connor Stone and Alexandre Adam, under the MIT license.
Niagara uses Caskade's public Module, Param, ActiveContext and OverrideParam APIs.
The Caskade copyright and MIT license are retained in LICENSE.

Caustics supplies the scientific lensing and image simulators. The inference
example follows its image-fitting tutorial with a 21-parameter model:
https://github.com/Ciela-Institute/caustics
https://caustics.readthedocs.io/en/latest/examples/Example_ImageFit_MCMC.html

PyTorch provides tensor computation, differentiation, FX, functional transforms
and compiler backends. These libraries remain separately installed dependencies.

